DOCUMENT();
loadMacros(
"PGstandard.pl",
"MathObjects.pl",
"PGML.pl"
);
Context("Numeric");
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstantFunctions=>0);
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstants=>0);

$fun_2 = Formula("(ln(x))/6");
$fun_1 = Formula("ln((x^2-2*x+3))");

Context("Interval");

$set_ans_3 = Compute("((9, infinity) - ({-2, 4}))");
$set_ans_4 = Compute("(9, infinity) U (9, infinity)");
$set_ans_1 = Compute("{-8, -4, 0, 1, 7} U {-9, 4}");
$set_ans_2 = Compute("[7, infinity) U {-9, 4}");

Context("Vector");

BEGIN_PGML
# Questions:

_For arithmetic problems, if the result is not an integer, then retain *three significant digits*._

[`3+6.16+1*8`] is equal to [_____]{Formula('17.16')}
---

[`2.57+6.37+9-19/8`] is equal to [_____]{Formula('15.565')}
---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{x | x \geq 7\}`]
- [`B = \{-9, 4\}`]
- [`C = \{-8, -4, 0, 1, 7\}`]

Compute:
- [`C \cup B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_1}
- [`A \cup B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_2}

---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{-2, 4\}`]
- [`B = \{x | x > 8\}`]

Compute:
- [`B - (A) = `] [_____]{$set_ans_3}
- [`B \cup B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_4}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle 9, -7, 4 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle -9, 2, -5 \rangle `]

Compute:
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-9, 2, -5>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- [` \vec{v} \cdot \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-9, 2, -5>") . Compute("<9, -7, 4>")}
- [` \vec{u} \cdot \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<9, -7, 4>") . Compute("<-9, 2, -5>")}
- [` \left\| \vec{v} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<-9, 2, -5>"))}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<-9, 2, -5>"))}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle -6, -5, -5 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle -3, 10, 2 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{w} = \langle -5, 7, -2 \rangle `]

Compute:
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<-3, 10, 2>"))}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<-6, -5, -5>"))}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-3, 10, 2>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- [` \vec{u} \times \vec{w} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-6, -5, -5>") x Compute("<-5, 7, -2>")}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{w} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-5, 7, -2>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- [` \vec{w} \cdot \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-5, 7, -2>") . Compute("<-6, -5, -5>")}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_1]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->D()}
- [`f'(5) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->eval(x=>5)}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_2]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()}
- [`f'(8) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->eval(x=>8)}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->D()}

---
END_PGML
ENDDOCUMENT();
